      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.66,
      "end": 2.77,
      "text": "Hey, how's it going? You doing okay?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.33,
      "end": 16.65,
      "text": "A sketch is usually quick and loose, catching an idea. A study is more focused, it's practice for a specific part, like a hand or the light on a vase."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.96,
      "end": 23.81,
      "text": "Ha, in a way. It's how artists solve a problem before the real painting."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.48,
      "end": 37.77,
      "text": "Then do a few cloud studies first. Small ones, maybe ten minutes each, from photos or the real sky."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.87,
      "end": 50.22,
      "text": "Look at where the light hits and where the cloud is darkest underneath. Clouds are mostly about soft edges and value."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 54.61,
      "end": 58.52,
      "text": "Enjoy it. Ten small studies will teach you more than one big struggle."
    }
  ]
